node_modules
dist
coverage
npm-debug.log*
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
test
*.md
# ...but the drill library IS .md content the API serves (ADR-0029). The
# pattern above happens not to match it — `*` does not cross `/` — so this
# currently survives by accident. Stated explicitly so a later tidy-up to
# `**/*.md` cannot silently empty the library: nest build would copy
# nothing, readdirSync would throw into its catch, and production would
# serve an empty shelf behind a green CI.
!src/drills/library/*.md
.eslintcache
